<description>
Emit blue perpendicular guide lines from each green marker and stamp blue rings where they cross the red guide lines.

Input structure
- The background is dominant, with full-span parallel red guide lines.
- Each source marker is a green 3x3 ring centered on a red guide-line pixel.
- All guide lines are horizontal or all guide lines are vertical.

Rule
- A marker on a horizontal red line emits a vertical blue line through its center column; a marker on a vertical red line emits a horizontal blue line through its center row.
- The emitted line paints only background cells blue.
- At each crossing with a red guide line, stamp a blue 3x3 ring with the red center preserved; keep the original green source marker unchanged.

Key insight
- The green ring is not copied along the red line; it defines the perpendicular projection, and every red-line crossing on that projection receives the same ring shape in blue.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "green 3x3 marker rings centered on full-span red guide lines",
  "path": "full row or column through each marker center, perpendicular to the orientation of the red guide lines",
  "trajectory": "paint background cells on the path blue",
  "transform": "at every red guide-line crossing on the path, paint a blue 3x3 ring with the red center preserved; keep original green marker rings unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10-16 rows x 10-18 cols, background BLACK(0)
  colors: input uses RED(2)+GREEN(3) on BLACK; output adds BLUE(1)
  guide_lines:
    orientation: all horizontal OR all vertical (full-span, single-pixel)
    count: 1-4
    color: RED(2), spanning the entire row/column
    spacing: >=3 between adjacent lines (observed 4-6)
    border_clearance: each line >=1 from grid edge (for ring fit)
  markers:
    count: 1-2
    shape: 3x3 GREEN(3) ring with RED(2) center, centered on a guide line
    placement: each marker on a different guide line; marker center >=1 from grid edge
    perpendicular_coords: unique across markers, >=3 apart [observed]
  output_transform:
    emit: from each marker center, draw a full-span BLUE line perpendicular to guide-line orientation (paint only BLACK cells)
    crossing_rings: at each intersection of emitted BLUE line with a guide line (excluding the marker itself), stamp a 3x3 BLUE ring with RED center preserved
    marker_preserved: original GREEN marker rings unchanged
  non_overlap: all 3x3 rings (markers + crossing rings) pairwise non-overlapping (Chebyshev dist >=3 between centers)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid dims (10-16 x 10-18) and orientation (H or V).
    2. Place 1-4 guide lines along the chosen axis, each >=1 from border, pairwise spacing >=4.
    3. Pick 1-2 marker positions, each on a distinct guide line, center >=1 from all edges.
       Ensure perpendicular coords are >=3 apart (so crossing rings on the same line don't overlap).
    4. For each marker, compute crossing points on all other guide lines.
       Verify all ring centers (markers + crossings) have pairwise Chebyshev dist >=3.
    5. Fill guide lines with RED. Place GREEN 3x3 marker rings. This is the INPUT.
    6. To build OUTPUT: paint emitted BLUE perpendicular lines (only on BLACK cells), stamp BLUE 3x3 crossing rings (preserving RED centers), keep GREEN markers.
```
